title:: MITHRatiosView
summary:: A window visualization for MITHScreenRatios
related:: Classes/MITHScreenRatios
categories:: geometry, gui, scbook

description::
Creates a window with dimensions based on a MITHScreenRatios instance. The window displays a rectangle with the specified ratio and can be resized while maintaining the proper update notifications to the model.

classmethods::

method:: new
Creates a new MITHRatiosView.
argument:: model
A MITHScreenRatios instance to use as the model
argument:: win
Optional existing window to use (default: creates a new window)
returns:: MITHRatiosView instance (actually returns the window)

instancemethods::

private:: init, makeWindow

method:: model
Returns the associated MITHScreenRatios model.
returns:: MITHScreenRatios

method:: win
Returns the window being used.
returns:: Window

method:: update
Responds to changes in the model, particularly viewDims changes.
argument:: obj
The object that changed
argument:: what
The changed aspect (e.g., \viewDims)
argument:: val
The new value
returns:: this

examples::

code::
// Create a MITHScreenRatios instance
m = MITHScreenRatios.new;

// Create a view with default dimensions
v = MITHRatiosView(m);

// Change to golden ratio dimensions
m.viewDims_(m.ratioToDims(\phi, 800));

// Try some other ratios
m.viewDims_(m.ratioToDims(\r3_2, 600));  // Perfect fifth
m.viewDims_(m.ratioToDims(\r16_9, 800));  // HDTV

// Create a view in an existing window
w = Window("Custom Window", Rect(100, 100, 400, 300)).front;
v = MITHRatiosView(m, w);

// Alternative using the gui method
m = MITHScreenRatios.new;
v = m.gui;
::